 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 543081,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine  whether each graph is connected or disconnected and identify the set of vertices that make up each of its components.\n<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7a3a803609fc3586.png\" alt=\"Six graphs. Each graph has four vertices: a, b, c, and d. Graph F: edges connect d c and d a. Graph G: edges connect a b, a d, and d c. Graph H: edges connect d c, d a, and c b. Graph I: edges connect d c, c b, d a, and a b. Graph J: edges connect a d and c b. Graph K: an edge connects b and d.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A graph is connected if it has only one component. Graphs G, H, and I are connected; so, they each have a single component with the vertices {<i>a, b, c, d</i>}.</p>\n<p>A graph is disconnected if it has more than one component. Graph F is disconnected with two components: {<i>a, c, d</i>} and {<i>b</i>}. Graph J is disconnected with two components: {<i>a, d</i>} and {<i>b, c</i>}. Graph K is disconnected with three components: {<i>a</i>}, {<i>b, d</i>}, and {<i>c</i>}.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Graphs <i>G</i>, <i>H</i>, and <i>I</i> are connected; so, they each have a single component with the vertices {<i>a</i>, <i>b</i>, <i>c</i>, <i>d</i>}. Graph <i>F</i> is disconnected with two components, {<i>a</i>, <i>c</i>, <i>d</i>} and {<i>b</i>}. Graph <i>J</i> is disconnected with two components, {<i>a</i>, <i>d</i>} and {<i>b</i>, <i>c</i>}. Graph <i>K</i> is disconnected with three components, {<i>a</i>}, {<i>b</i>, <i>d</i>}, and {<i>c</i>}."
    }
   ],
